@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed guarded local command and duplicate result lookup
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Caller
participant "Web / owner handler" as H
participant "Current authority" as A
database "Owned records / command result / pending intent" as DB
Caller -> H : intended mutation + command identity + expected version
H -> A : verify current actor / resource / action
A --> H : scoped context or denial
alt permitted intent
 H -> DB : begin guarded transaction; compare prior command intent
 alt matching duplicate with permitted prior result
  DB --> H : actual recorded result
 else new command and valid current guards
  H -> DB : mutate owned state + result + required pending intent
  DB --> H : committed result or explicit conflict
 end
 H --> Caller : actual local result / pending reference
else denied / invalid
 H --> Caller : safe refusal; no admitted mutation
end
note over H,DB
 No provider/runner call while holding the local transaction.
 Lost response resolves the same command; it is not proof of rollback.
 Concrete grant/version/uniqueness guards remain evaluated implementation work.
end note
@enduml
